dman (D) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term Democrat Eugene Vindman defends a Northern Virginia seat that leans Democratic by about two points, facing Republican Doug Ollivant, a political newcomer who won the August primary. Vindman has raised over $12 million and holds $6.6 million on hand, dwarfing Ollivant's roughly $250,000 in receipts, with negligible outside spending on either side so far.\n\nNo public general-election polling is available, but ten expert raters place the race at Likely D or better, and prediction markets give Vindman a 94-96% chance of winning. Campaign coverage has centered on affordability, jobs, and data-center growth. The race appears out of reach for Republicans barring a major shift in the national environment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.972, "margin": 13.04}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9562, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9664, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9585, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9406, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9612, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9637, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9667, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9827, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9791, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9746, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9559, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9685, "margin": 13.0}]}